{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber","id":993312,"title":"Mana Management, or Are You A Mana-Hungry Tass-Grabber?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T21:43:38-07:00","id":993312,"title":"Mana Management, or Are You A Mana-Hungry Tass-Grabber?","content":"I wanted to ask a few questions about how you find the Mana supply working in your games.<br /> <br /> I'm coming from a Werewolf game where Loci offer a lot more Essence than Hallows do Mana. Despite that, our last game had unreliable access to Loci and we found most of our Essence coming from other sources.<br /> <br /> How much Mana do people seem to use, per session? What are their most common methods of getting Mana back? Hallow seems limited, especially with the other nice Merits though once you've got a Legacy Oblations seem the easiest method. Supernal Revelation and Exceptional Successes seem nice but uncommon unless you're more or less built for it, and lets pretend you're not the spamming-praxes type. Scouring looks like it would be a great method in an easy-going game that skips a few days, allowing characters to gain the Mana without suffering the penalty during playtime. Has anyone had mages resort to Blood Sacrifice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:20:58-07:00","id":993321,"title":"","content":"Mana is one of those things that sits around for a while and then goes all at once. When it goes, it usually stays gone for quite a while, because it's usually in the middle of an adventure and no-one has time to sit around praying to their ancestors for an hour. You can generally find ways to recharge during downtime but, during play, you're stuck with tass and familiars for the most part.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've wanted to try the blood sacrifice thing with a Thyrsus. It seems far less ethically dubious when you actually eat the animal after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:27:05-07:00","id":993325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=993321#post993321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've wanted to try the blood sacrifice thing with a Thyrsus. It seems far less ethically dubious when you actually eat the animal after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, I'm surprised sacrificing an animal is considered an Act of Hubris, it doesn't seem to fit in the listed Acts of Hubris. Or do you rule animals as an exception?<br /> <br /> Thanks for letting me know about the Mana, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:49:56-07:00","id":993333,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of needlessly inflicting pain is where Hubris comes into it, but that really depends on what you're doing. I've seen animals be slaughtered for food in ways that, to my mind, were less humane than ways I've seen them slaughtered for sacrifice (and vice versa). Usually, sacrifices are eaten after, as well, so, as long as the animal is slaughtered humanely, it's not any ethically worse than making a meal.<br /> <br /> To my mind, anyway.<br /> <br /> And no problem on the Mana flow thing. It's always interesting to watch. Personally, I actually wish Mana couldn't be acquired by tearing it out of the Tapestry with Prime or taking it from familiars; makes it a bit more valuable and prevents two Paths from basically bypassing the cost of Mana entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:30:10-07:00","id":993948,"title":"","content":"Three. Death can do both of those things.<br /> <br /> Actually four. Mind can also do familiars. <br /> <br /> Poor Acanthus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-27-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:48:33-07:00","id":993951,"title":"","content":"Acanthus can just go back in time to before they harvested the mana and harvest it again for the very first time. So 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:41:51-07:00","id":994036,"title":"","content":"Please try to keep it on topic. Have either of you had any experience with Mana shortages or surplus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:04:59-07:00","id":994053,"title":"","content":"I haven't, but one of my players has been spending mana left and right to buy down Paradox so it can definitely happen. I expect it will happen less often as the game progresses though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:08:33-07:00","id":994056,"title":"","content":"I've tended to find that mana Isn't a problem for me. Though I tend to scour to keep myself topped up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:00:45-07:00","id":994233,"title":"","content":"Regular and low level scouring to maintain full Mana Pool. Keeping regular Mana usage low (by mainly casting within Superior Arcanum) means the reserves are topped off for when it counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:43:17-07:00","id":994280,"title":"","content":"Given that two out of the four players in my group are new to Mage and the ST feels as if he has a lot on his plate without trying to keep track of every single number, we basically start each session with a full mana pool. That being said, we usually don't get any mana during the sessions, so mana usage is definitely a thing. I probably spend the most since I know the game the best out of my group. I also tend to push my spellcasting a bit more than the others. I was the first to risk paradox, both chance die and higher.<br /> <br /> We get the vast majority of our mana from our hallow. We also tend to have large gaps in the game time, so we do tend to either be topped off or close to full. <br /> <br /> And no, we definitely haven't had anyone even consider a sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T02:22:13-07:00","id":995125,"title":"","content":"As a member of a legacy, I find myself gaining something like 3-4 mana every day. At this point, I have about 35 mana worth of tass stored here and there, and the main reason I don't have more is because I stopped stockpiling it because I almost never use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:17:18-07:00","id":995183,"title":"","content":"Yeah, once you join a Legacy, you basically opt out of the Mana economy, by and large.<br /> <br /> Still, that much tass in one place feels like it should have an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:06:22-07:00","id":995201,"title":"","content":"Well, once you have a surplus you start investing it in more valuable stuff, like Sleepwalkers with Imbued items, brand new Mages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:13:04-07:00","id":995204,"title":"","content":"A large pile of Tass is the natural state of an unclaimed Hallow. It just accumulates [dots x3] manaworth of the stuff and clogs up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:33:18-07:00","id":996297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=994280#post994280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that two out of the four players in my group are new to Mage and the ST feels as if he has a lot on his plate without trying to keep track of every single number, we basically start each session with a full mana pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a thing you can do, but I might recommend you try doing it the old fashioned way - it makes your playstyle very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:21:40-07:00","id":996411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=995201#post995201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, once you have a surplus you start investing it in more valuable stuff, like Sleepwalkers with Imbued items, brand new Mages, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. I keep my apprentice and myself fully supplied with mana, and I use it to power my imbued/enhanced items and to allow me to just burn through mysteries by throwing mana at the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:48:35-07:00","id":997922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=996297#post996297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's certainly a thing you can do, but I might recommend you try doing it the old fashioned way - it makes your playstyle very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really my decision to make. That and we haven't played in like, 4 months, soooo...yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:17:27-07:00","id":998072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=997922#post997922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really my decision to make. That and we haven't played in like, 4 months, soooo...yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing to recommend next time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:49:13-08:00","id":1009519,"title":"","content":"During my chronicle I had a rule that you only received Hallow mana during downtime once per week, to represent the fact that you used the other 6 Mana for your usual day to day activities.<br /> <br /> For awhile our Acanthus was light on Mana because he used a lot of Mana heavy spells and he sacrificed animals in &quot;Voodoo&quot; rituals on a fairly regular basis.<br /> <br /> Btw, this was a 1e chronicle. I'm curious whether my downtime rule would be too harsh in the new 2e mana economy. I'd be interested in hearing opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:27:34-08:00","id":1009534,"title":"","content":"It's kind of assumed that between stories a Mage is able to replenish his mana and WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:54:28-08:00","id":1009606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993312-mana-management-or-are-you-a-mana-hungry-tass-grabber?p=1009519#post1009519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During my chronicle I had a rule that you only received Hallow mana during downtime once per week, to represent the fact that you used the other 6 Mana for your usual day to day activities.<br /> <br /> For awhile our Acanthus was light on Mana because he used a lot of Mana heavy spells and he sacrificed animals in &quot;Voodoo&quot; rituals on a fairly regular basis.<br /> <br /> Btw, this was a 1e chronicle. I'm curious whether my downtime rule would be too harsh in the new 2e mana economy. I'd be interested in hearing opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair rule. I've noticed Storytellers seem to be lenient towards mages, but it doesn't hurt the game to just go by the rules as is. If they do need Mana, there's ways to get it in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-28-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:31:07-08:00","id":1009775,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I've never been quite sure what a Mage would need to spend Mana on during their downtime. I guess it depends what is you're up to in your off-time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}